                "event": "Flood Watch",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 25 at 11:29PM MDT until September 26 at 3:00AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of east-central and southeast New Mexico,\nincluding the following areas, in central New Mexico, Eastern\nLincoln County and South Central Mountains. In east central New\nMexico, Quay, Curry, Roosevelt, and De Baca Counties. In southeast\nNew Mexico, Chaves County Plains and Southwest Chaves County.\n\n* WHEN...Until 3 AM MDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nCreeks and streams may rise out of their banks. Flooding may occur\nin poor drainage and urban areas. Low-water crossings may be\nflooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- A swath of heavy rain over the past 24 hours over southeast New\nMexico will elevate the risk for any new storms over the area to\nproduce flash flooding through this evening.\n- Rapid runoff and flash flooding will be most likely in complex\nterrain, below recent burn scars, low-lying areas, urban areas,\nnormally dry arroyos, near rivers and streams, and in locations\nwhere the ground is already saturated from recent heavy rainfall.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued. Never drive through flood\nwaters. Most flash flood deaths occur in automobiles.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
